            "notes": "identifier/ontology_id CHEBI:18290 -> CHEBI:9532. ChEBI's live definition of CHEBI:18290 is 'an organic CHLORIDE SALT of thiamine(1+) diphosphate' \u2014 a counterion this record's label never mentions. CHEBI:9532 is the compound itself; 'pyrophosphate' and 'diphosphate' are the same moiety under two naming conventions, hence SYNONYM_MATCH. The term was freed by moving the 0.2% stock solution to a minted identifier per #288. The existing SSSOM row already flagged this as 'SYMMETRIC: charge/protonation/ester variant'."
          }
        ]
